    "q-75239": {
      "dom_id": "step-q75239",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -23 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+23{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{2}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$ \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-75239-a",
